## Section headers and homepage cards

The 7 section landing pages and the Colour, Data and Illustration guides each have an original header. Each one explains its section: typography and swatches for Styles, controls for Components, a connected sequence of steps for Patterns. Detailed component pages leave the space for working examples.

The Styles, Components and Patterns cards on the homepage reuse the shapes of their section header. Keep the two matched when either changes.

- A header is 640 by 480 and a homepage card is 320 by 140.
- Show the whole header without cropping or stretching.
- On wide screens, put it beside the heading and introduction, with a minimum height of 450 pixels. On narrow screens, put it below them.
- Do not put headings in the image.

These headers repeat the introduction beside them, so they have empty alternative text. Their pale background does not change with a household’s theme colour.

<h2 id="bg-ill-09">Use invented households</h2>

Use invented names, rooms and devices in every public example. Before you share a screenshot of a real dashboard, remove access tokens, exact home locations, faces, number plates and any names the task does not need.

Get permission from anyone who can be identified, and for any photo someone else supplied. Record who holds the rights. A photo being public is not permission.

Presence avatars and camera previews are personal. Do not add faces or show a precise location to make a dashboard feel more personal.
